{"type":"message","id":"397d50af","parentId":"a3c30022","timestamp":"2026-02-02T16:45:05.963Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are setting up and running the BluePrint construction document analysis pipeline for a new project: **HHC Bellevue Hospital — Ambulance Drop Off Renovation**.\n\n**Project location:** /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/\n\n**Source files (already downloaded):**\n/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/BluePrint/\n- 11202402_Drawings_Part1 (1).pdf through Part7\n- 11202402_Specifications (1).pdf  \n- IFB - HHC PART 1 (1).pdf\n\n**Reference project for pipeline structure:**\n/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/usps-greenwich/ — follow the same folder structure and output formats.\n\n**PHASE 1: PDF Extraction**\n1. Create directories: drawings/, drawings/pages/, drawings/text/, drawings/extracted/, specs/, synthesis/\n2. For EACH drawing PDF (Parts 1-7), extract pages as PNG images using Python (pdf2image/poppler at 150 DPI to keep file sizes manageable — these are big files). Save to drawings/pages/ as page_NNN.png with continuous numbering across all parts.\n3. Extract text layers from each page. Save to drawings/text/page_NNN.txt\n4. Create drawings/manifest.json tracking all pages with metadata.\n5. Extract specs PDF text — save raw text to specs/specs_raw_text.json organized by section.\n\n**PHASE 2: Sheet Classification**\n1. For each drawing page, determine the sheet number and discipline (G=General, C=Civil, A=Architectural, S=Structural, M=Mechanical, E=Electrical, P=Plumbing, FP=Fire Protection, etc.)\n2. Create drawings/classification.json and a sheet_index.json mapping sheet numbers to page files.\n3. Identify key sheets: floor plans, demo plans, finish plans, door schedules, partition types, reflected ceiling plans.\n\n**PHASE 3: IFB/Bid Sheet Parsing**  \n1. Extract the IFB PDF text\n2. Parse the bid breakdown / line items into bid_breakdown.json — each item needs: item number, description, unit (SF/LF/EA/LS), and a blank quantity field\n3. Create takeoff_checklist.md listing all items that need quantities\n\n**PHASE 4: Specifications Summary**\n1. Parse specs into CSI divisions\n2. Create specs/specs_summary.json with section numbers, titles, and key requirements\n3. Flag any ICRA (Infection Control Risk Assessment) requirements — this is a renovation inside an operational hospital\n\n**PHASE 5: Initial Synthesis**\n1. Create synthesis/project_summary.md (follow USPS Greenwich format)\n2. Create synthesis/rooms.json — all rooms identified from floor plans\n3. Create synthesis/scope_by_trade.json — scope broken down by CSI division\n4. Create synthesis/flags.json — discrepancies, missing info, things Doug should know\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n- Use Python for PDF processing (pymupdf/fitz for text, pdf2image for images)\n- Install any missing packages with pip\n- This is a hospital renovation — look for phasing requirements, ICRA, infection control barriers, negative air pressure requirements\n- The project number appears to be 11202402\n- Be thorough but prioritize getting through all phases. If a phase is taking too long, save progress and move on.\n- Write a final STATUS.md at the project root summarizing what was completed and what's pending.\n\nStart with Phase 1 and work through sequentially. This is a big project — take your time and do it right."}],"timestamp":1770050705961}}
{"type":"message","id":"0645db45","parentId":"397d50af","timestamp":"2026-02-02T16:45:12.312Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to set up and run a BluePrint construction document analysis pipeline for the HHC Bellevue Hospital project. This is a comprehensive multi-phase task that involves:\n\n1. PDF extraction (drawings and specs)\n2. Sheet classification\n3. IFB/Bid Sheet parsing\n4. Specifications summary\n5. Initial synthesis\n\nLet me start by exploring the project structure and the reference project to understand the expected output format, then begin Phase 1.\n\nI'll need to:\n1. First check the existing project structure\n2. Look at the reference project (usps-greenwich) for format guidance\n3. Set up directories\n4. Install necessary Python packages\n5. Extract PDFs (images and text)\n6. Continue through all phases\n\nLet me start by exploring what's already there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by exploring the project structure and the reference project to understand the expected formats, then work through all phases systematically."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/BluePrint/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/usps-greenwich/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"moonshot","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":7665,"output":293,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7958,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770050705962}}
