{"type":"message","id":"9257148b","parentId":"850b9cea","timestamp":"2026-02-02T16:45:16.025Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USPS Greenwich, CT — MIP Renovation\n## Project Summary (Phase 2 Synthesis — Full Run)\n\n**Project:** USPS - Greenwich, CT - MIP (Modernization Improvement Program)  \n**Address:** 29 Valley Drive, Greenwich, CT 06831  \n**Owner:** United States Postal Service  \n**Architect:** WJP, Low Design Inc (WSP USA — Civil, MEP)  \n**Project Number:** 083060G03  \n**Contract Number:** 104267-21-B-0030  \n**Status:** Issued for Construction (12/17/25)  \n**Synthesis Date:** 2025-01-29  \n**Sheets Processed:** 41 of 41 pages (100%)\n\n---\n\n## Building Overview\n\nSingle-story USPS post office facility undergoing full interior modernization (MIP renovation). Scope encompasses selective demolition of existing finishes, fixtures, and select partitions, followed by complete interior renovation of operational spaces (workroom, platforms), support spaces (restrooms, locker rooms, breakroom), and public-facing areas (lobby, foyer, window clerks). Exterior scope includes masonry/surface cleaning and site work (asphalt overlay, pavement markings, erosion control).\n\n## Rooms Identified (30 total)\n\n### Numbered Rooms (20)\n| Room # | Room Name | Finish Data | Demo Scope |\n|--------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n| 100 | WORKROOM | ✅ Complete | Ceiling, lights, equipment |\n| 101 | BREAKROOM | ✅ Complete | Carpet, ceiling, casework, fixtures |\n| 102 | CUSTODIAL ROOM | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 103 | WOMEN'S LOCKER ROOM | ❌ Pending | Floor tile, VWF, ceiling, fixtures, lockers, plumbing |\n| 104 | WOMEN'S RESTROOM | ❌ Pending | Floor tile, VWF, ceiling, fixtures, plumbing |\n| 105 | MENS RESTROOM | ❌ Pending | Floor tile, VWF, ceiling, fixtures, plumbing |\n| 106 | MEN'S LOCKER ROOM | ❌ Pending | Floor tile, VWF, ceiling, fixtures, lockers |\n| 107 | SUPERVISOR'S OFFICE | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 108 | VESTIBULE | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 109 | CIO ROOM | ❌ Pending | New ductless AC |\n| 110 | MAIL PLATFORM | ❌ Pending | Traffic doors, lights (21' ceiling) |\n| 110A | GENERAL OFFICE | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 111 | WOMEN'S LOCKER ROOM | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 114 | WOMEN'S RESTROOM | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 115 | MAIL PLATFORM | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 116 | VESTIBULE | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 118 | VESTIBULE | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 119 | ELECTRICAL ROOM | ❌ Pending | Panel upgrades |\n| 126 | EEO ROOM | ❌ Pending | — |\n| 170 | PLATFORM | ❌ Pending | Traffic doors, lights (27' ceiling) |\n\n### Unnamed Spaces (10)\nLOBBY, FOYER, POSTMASTER OFFICE, WINDOW CLERKS, SUPPLY ROOM, VAULT, REGISTRY CAGE (✅ has finishes), P.O. BOX, ELEV., STAIRCASE(S)\n\n## Finish Schedule (3 rooms extracted from A-600)\n\n| Room | Floor | Base | Wall | Ceiling | Ceiling Ht |\n|------|-------|------|------|---------|------------|\n| WORKROOM (100) | CONC. SEALER | WB-1 | P-1/P-2/P-5 | ACT-1 | 9'-0\" AFF |\n| BREAKROOM (101) | RFT-1 | WB-1 | P-1/P-2/P-5 | ACT-1 | 9'-0\" AFF |\n| REGISTRY CAGE | RFT-1 | WB-1 | P-1 | GWB-1 | 9'-0\" AFF |\n\n> ⚠️ **Only 3 of ~30 rooms extracted.** A-600 re-extraction needed for complete schedule.\n\n### Finish Legend\n- **CONC. SEALER** — Polished/sealed concrete (03 35 43 / 09 96 11)\n- **RFT-1** — Resilient floor tile (09 65 01)\n- **WB-1** — Rubber/vinyl wall base (09 65 01)\n- **P-1** — Paint standard (09 91 00)\n- **P-2** — Paint accent/secondary (09 91 00)\n- **P-5** — High-performance coating (09 96 11)\n- **ACT-1** — Acoustical ceiling tile 2x4, 5/8\" thick, vinyl faced (09 51 13) — Armstrong/USG/CertainTeed\n- **GWB-1** — Gypsum wallboard ceiling (09 29 00)\n\n## Door Schedule (4 doors extracted from A-600)\n\n| Door # | Type | Material | Finish | Frame | Hardware |\n|--------|------|----------|--------|-------|----------|\n| 100J | SINGLE | HM | P-2 | STEEL | EXIST |\n| 100A | PR (Pair) | HM | P-2 | HM | — |\n| 100B | PR (Pair) | HM | P-2 | HM | — |\n| 100C | PR (Pair) | HM | P-2 | HM | — |\n\n> ⚠️ **Only 4 doors captured.** Full door and hardware schedules need re-extraction.\n\n## Demolition Scope\n\n### Interior Demo (20 keynotes from AD102/AD104)\n| Category | Keynotes | Description |\n|----------|----------|-------------|\n| Floor Removal | D1.2, D1.4, D1.5 | Carpet, VWF, floor tile |\n| Wall Removal | D2.5, D2.6 | Partitions (partial and full-height) |\n| Door Removal | D2.1, D2.2, D3.2 | Door+frame, door only, traffic door panel |\n| Ceiling Removal | D6.1, D6.3, D6.4, D6.5, D6.7, D6.10 | Full ceiling, grid, tile, lights, soffit |\n| Fixture/Equip Removal | D5.1, D5.3, D5.4, D5.6, D5.7, D4.5 | Equipment, accessories, plumbing, casework, lockers, lights |\n\n### Plumbing Demo (5 items from PD-100)\nWater closets, urinals, lavatories, sinks, electric water cooler\n\n### Exterior Cleaning (6 items from A-200)\nWalls, stairs, ramps, overhead doors, dock levelers, metal panels + test clean requirement\n\n### Demo Rooms with Enlarged Plans (AD102)\n101 (Breakroom), 102 (Lockers), 103 (Lockers), 104 (Restroom), 105 (Restroom), 106 (Supervisor's Office)\n\n## Partition Types\n\n| Code | Description | Status |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| G6S-0A | 3-5/8\" steel studs, 20ga, 24\" OC, 5/8\" GWB ea. side | ✅ Spec-derived |\n| A-1 | TBD — legend not extracted | ❌ Pending |\n| A-2 | TBD — legend not extracted | ❌ Pending |\n| A-3 | TBD — legend not extracted | ❌ Pending |\n| A-4 | TBD — legend not extracted | ❌ Pending |\n\n### Key GWB Spec Requirements (09 29 00)\n- Standard studs: 24\" OC | Security: 16\" OC\n- Moisture-resistant GWB at wet areas\n- Glass-mat backing board behind tile\n- Security barrier mesh with clips 10-12\" OC\n- Finish Level 4 (flat paint), Level 5 (semi-gloss/gloss paint)\n- Seismic bracing required for ACT and GWB ceilings (A-501 details)\n\n### Ceiling Heights from RCP (A-101)\n- **9'-0\" AFF** — Standard offices, support rooms\n- **21'-0\" ±** — Mail Platform / Workroom high-bay (exposed structure)\n- **27'-0\" ±** — Platform 170 (exposed structure)\n\n## Scope by Trade (Doug's 6 Core)\n\n### 1. Demolition (Div 02)\nFull interior selective demo: floors, walls, ceilings, fixtures, equipment, lockers, doors. Asbestos abatement (02 82 33/36). Exterior cleaning. 20 demo keynotes + 5 plumbing demo + 6 exterior items.\n\n### 2. Concrete & Masonry (Div 03-04)\nConcrete patching at demo locations. Polished concrete/sealer at Workroom. Exterior masonry cleaning with test panel. CMU infill/repair. Site concrete (foundations, catch basins).\n\n### 3. Rough Carpentry / Framing / Drywall (Div 06-07, 09 GWB)\nMetal stud framing (5 partition types). GWB with 4 finish levels. Security mesh. Glass-mat backing. Blocking/backing. Firestopping (07 84 00). Joint sealants (07 92 00).\n\n### 4. Finish Carpentry / Doors / Specialties (Div 08, 10, 12)\nHM doors/frames/hardware. Traffic doors. Access doors. Automatic entrances. Window film. Toilet compartments. Lockers. Toilet accessories. Display boards/cases. Signage (interior + illuminated). Wire mesh. Wall protection. Fire extinguisher cabinets. Casework.\n\n### 5. Painting (09 91 00, 09 96 11)\nThree paint systems (P-1, P-2, P-5). Interior walls, ceilings, doors/frames. High-performance coatings at Workroom. Exposed structure at platforms. Exterior bollards.\n\n### 6. Flooring & Tiling (09 30 13, 09 51 13, 09 65 01)\nCeramic tile (floor + wall) at restrooms with crack isolation & waterproofing. Resilient floor tile (RFT-1) at office areas. ACT ceilings (ACT-1) with seismic bracing and fiberglass insulation. GWB ceilings (GWB-1). Wall base (WB-1).\n\n## Key Spec Sections (Priority Divisions)\n\n| Division | Key Sections |\n|----------|-------------|\n| 02 | Selective demo (02 41 13/19), Asbestos (02 82 33/36), Masonry removal (02 42 97) |\n| 03 | Concrete maintenance (03 01 30), Forming/reinforcement (03 10/20), Cast-in-place (03 30 00), Polished concrete (03 35 43) |\n| 04 | Masonry cleaning (04 01 10), Mortar/grout (04 05 14), CMU (04 22 00) |\n| 06 | Rough carpentry/EIFS repair (06 10 00) |\n| 07 | Firestopping (07 84 00), Joint sealants (07 92 00) |\n| 08 | HM doors/frames (08 11 00), Access doors (08 31 13), Sectional doors (08 36 13), Traffic doors (08 38 00), Auto entrances (08 42 29), Hardware (08 71 00), Glazing (08 80 00), Window film (08 87 00) |\n| 09 | GWB (09 29 00), Ceramic tile (09 30 13), ACT (09 51 13), Resilient flooring (09 65 01), Painting (09 91 00), Hi-perf coatings (09 96 11) |\n| 10 | Display boards (10 11 00), Display cases (10 12 00), Signage (10 14 04/14), Toilet comps (10 21 15), Wire mesh (10 22 13), Wall protection (10 26 00), Toilet accessories (10 28 13), Fire extinguishers (10 44 00), Lockers (10 51 13) |\n\n**Total spec sections indexed:** 849 across 21 divisions\n\n## MEP Coordination Notes\n\n- **Plumbing (P-series):** Fixture replacement in kind (WC, urinals, lavs, sink, EWC). New sanitary drainage routing. Trap primers. Cast iron sanitary/vent, Type L copper water.\n- **HVAC (M-series):** New ductless split AC for CIO Room (109). Condensing unit exterior mount. Field verify existing supply/return.\n- **Electrical (E-series):** Full LED lighting upgrade per ES601 fixture schedule (1x4, 2x4, pendant, recessed). Panel upgrades. Surge protection. Site lighting controls with photocell. New grounding system.\n\n## Flags & Considerations (22 total)\n\n### 🔴 Critical (3)\n1. **Incomplete finish schedule** — Only 3 of ~30 rooms extracted from A-600\n2. **Incomplete door schedule** — Only 4 doors captured\n3. **Partition type legend missing** — Types A-1 through A-4 unresolved\n\n### 🟡 Warning (11)\n4. Asbestos abatement required (02 82 33/36)\n5. Ceiling MEP coordination needed (multiple ceiling heights, ductless AC)\n6. Concrete sealer at Workroom — existing coating removal may be needed\n7. Plumbing fixture replacement requires finish coordination\n8. Security partition requirements at Vault/Registry\n9. Seismic bracing required for all ceilings\n10. Exterior test clean required before full cleaning\n11. Room numbering inconsistencies across disciplines\n12. 10 rooms without numbers\n13. Hardware schedule not extracted\n14. Equipment/responsibility matrix not found\n15. Site work scope — confirm if in this contract\n\n### 🔵 Info (4)\n16. Elevator likely owner-furnished\n17. Ductless split AC in CIO Room\n18. LED lighting upgrade throughout\n19. GWB Level 5 finish where semi-gloss/gloss paint scheduled\n\n## Data Completeness\n\n| Item | Status | Details |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| Sheets processed | 41/41 (100%) | All pages extracted |\n| Room inventory | 30 rooms/spaces | 20 numbered + 10 unnamed |\n| Finish schedule | 3 rooms (10%) | A-600 needs re-extraction |\n| Door schedule | 4 doors (~20%) | A-600 needs re-extraction |\n| Demo keynotes | 20 arch + 5 plumbing + 6 exterior | Complete |\n| Partition types | 5 identified, 1 detailed | Legend extraction needed |\n| Spec sections | 849 indexed, 21 divisions | Complete |\n| RCP data | ✅ Extracted (A-101) | 3 ceiling conditions identified |\n| Enlarged plans | ✅ A-400, A-401 | Restrooms, locker rooms, breakroom, CIO |\n| Detail sheets | ✅ A-500, A-501 | Signage, casework, ceiling details |\n| MEP coordination | ✅ All disciplines | Plumbing, HVAC, Electrical reviewed |\n| Civil/site | ✅ C-100 through C-500 | Asphalt, markings, erosion control |\n\n## Next Steps\n1. **Re-extract A-600** for complete finish schedule, door schedule, and hardware schedule\n2. **Extract partition type legend** from floor plan or detail sheet\n3. **Extract equipment schedule / responsibility matrix** from specs or drawings\n4. **Final merge** after remaining 6 pages (032, 035, 038-041) parallel extraction completes\n5. **Quantity takeoff** once all room finishes are resolved\n\n---\n\n*Generated by BluePrint Phase 2 synthesis (full run). 41 sheets processed, 849 spec sections indexed.*\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770050716024}}
{"type":"message","id":"c155ed51","parentId":"9257148b","timestamp":"2026-02-02T16:45:20.314Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a good understanding of the reference project structure and format. Now let me start creating the directories and setting up Phase 1. I'll need to:\n\n1. Create the directory structure\n2. Install necessary Python packages (pymupdf/fitz, pdf2image, poppler)\n3. Start extracting PDFs\n\nLet me begin.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the expected structure. Let me start **Phase 1: PDF Extraction** by creating the directory structure and installing necessary packages."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital && mkdir -p drawings/pages drawings/text drawings/extracted specs synthesis"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"pip install pymupdf pdf2image pillow --quiet"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"moonshot","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":13746,"output":172,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13918,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770050716025}}
